# Video and audio masters are large binary artifacts that no diff can read and
# that a checkout must never try to merge. They live in Git LFS so the object
# database stays clonable; the working tree still holds real bytes, so the
# digest gates in media/**/bin/verify-*.mjs verify exactly what they always did.
#
# CI note: no workflow currently runs check:film, check:rc1 or check:veo, which
# are the only gates that hash these files. Any workflow that starts running one
# MUST set `lfs: true` on actions/checkout, or it will hash pointer files and
# fail with a digest mismatch that looks like corrupted evidence.
*.mp4  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mov  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.wav  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.m4a  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.mp3  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
